 ## 2. UX Intent And Success
 
-- primary_user_intent: Know what is currently true, what remains open and who can perform the next step without reconciling contradictory sources or finding hidden invocation syntax.
-- success_signal: For a bound observation, current state and next operation agree across surfaces; supported routine actions use described contracts; completion and remaining obligations are trustworthy.
-- primary_decision_or_action: Inspect exact applicable material, perform an eligible operation, deliberately decide at the pending gate, request a permitted revision, recover a concrete failure or complete governance.
-- input_analysis: UX_INTENT_DEFINITION.md is ready; it is subordinate to the approved UR and this PRD upon approval.
-- benefit_boundary: Less search and manual bookkeeping are measured for defined scenarios. No claim that all code inspection disappears or every weaker model performs better.
+- primary_user_intent: Know what is currently true, read/discuss exact material, decide deliberately once and continue from a confirmed result; keep active context during an own-connection runtime switch.
+- success_signal: Same-bound current state/action agrees across consumers; supported operations are invocable without undocumented parser discovery; a replacement is qualified before new traffic, while old active work remains with its original owner and uncertain results remain inspectable.
+- primary_decision_or_action: Read the exact bound document, return/discuss in Chat, then approve eligible material by one primary button or exact text. With no outstanding approval, use the Core-permitted next step; later exact approval remains eligible for unchanged material. Inspect original operation on uncertainty. Tool permission and runtime replacement are not business approvals.
+- input_analysis: The renewed UX Intent Definition is analytically ready under the exact approved UR. It defines contextual action, native/Chat/remote and earliest-source intent with lifecycle recovery; it is not native usability success or technical design.
+- benefit_boundary: Defined routine scenarios measure search/manual/schema/follow-up/recovery burden. Ordinary engineering inspection is separated; model-specific improvement requires comparable actual model observations.
 
