+### 3.7 Owned runtime, retention and uncertainty execution detail
+
+Capture an occupancy event trace with owner epoch/generation/request/original operation IDs, reservation/start/qualification/admission/drain/close events, directly owned child handles and confirmed exits. Private IPC accepts only the SD-defined qualify/invoke/session_inspect/shutdown envelope; malformed, wrong-owner or wrong-generation results reject. Check actual tool/resource/SDK manifests before admission, including disabled group/app-only capabilities and the existing schema budgets (8 KiB per tool, 24 KiB aggregate including facade; 64 KiB input, 1 MiB result). Keep existing ten-second command worker timeout; qualification is bounded at thirty seconds and close wait at ten. Exceeding close wait leaves a counted protected close-unconfirmed generation. Qualification/capacity/end tests use actual direct child processes as well as deterministic fault injection; source mocks alone are not process exit proof.
+
+Pin open read and decision sessions, document resource paths, active executor work and unresolved business effects to the original generation. A switched current pointer affects only new admitted work. Test replacement while an approval acknowledgement is lost: inspect the original business UUID and actual receipt without resubmission, migration or creating a new approval. Test candidate failure with both usable and dead old current; an unavailable old path is not labelled preserved. The runtime-control receipt is ephemeral connection state, not another durable business ledger. External Codex termination is separately observed as external interruption; no claim of graceful close or rollback follows.
+
+Under the existing publication lock assert canonical real digest-addressed roots, verified immutable manifests and claims acquired before delayed module/resource load or direct spawn. Concurrent independent facades sharing a root must retain all protected paths. Confirmed own end permits releasing only its claim; unknown/foreign/legacy/crashed claims and unclaimed legacy roots remain conservative. No broad installation migration, age/PID garbage collection or new global process registry. Record exact retained/deleted own paths and protected hashes. A failure here prevents rollout; do not replace ownership proof with path equality.
