 - A clarification after approval that does not change approved scope, behavior or acceptance may be attributed as run evidence without changing the approved PRD. The no-mode `run-revise --run <run_id> --revision <revision_id>` remains the early PRD-to-SD revision path before downstream artefacts are linked. It requires a revised PRD, new `run-present` and a new deliberate `Approval: PRD`.
 - At valid active structured `CD+Tests` after exact approved UR/PRD/SD/TP and preparation, late source revision uses explicit `run-revise --preview`, then `--apply` with the same target/run/revision, reviewed proposal, operation UUID and preview digest. The earliest changed UR/PRD/SD/TP revokes its current approval and all dependent source approvals. Exact upstream approvals may remain; uncertain or contradictory impact requires clarification before application. QA/UAT/OR, awaiting CR, closed, damaged or pending states are outside this path.
-- Late apply archives the exact previous sources, mappings, presentations and Run before its atomic commit. Append-only `Source Revisions` in the sealed Run determine invalidated bindings; archive files are historical evidence only. Old files, approvals, replies and presentations never authorize renewal. Draft and record the affected sources through their current owners, present them afresh and obtain new deliberate approvals.
-- UR revision requires fresh post-UR Review/Mode and required UX. Later source revision retains only reviewed exact applicable analytical inputs; reassessment routes existing owners before dependent source authoring. Every late revision clears preparation, CD+Tests and review fulfillment; retained code/tests require fresh assessment under the renewed TP. Read-only inspection never recovers. Use explicit `--inspect`/`--recover` for the exact pending operation; a replay reports its historical effect separately from current state and grants no approval.
+- The same explicit preview/apply owner also supports UR revision in an active structured Run at SD with exact approved UR/PRD and a linked, reviewed draft SD, before SD approval, linked TP, implementation, reviews or closeout. Its reviewed proposal binds the current UR/PRD/SD sources, marks applicable analyses for reassessment and returns the same Run to UR. Other early source gates and lifecycle cases remain unsupported; the no-mode PRD boundary is unchanged. This Core/CLI capability does not add a model-callable MCP write tool.
+- Source revision apply archives the exact previous sources, mappings, presentations (including pending SD cards) and Run before its atomic commit. Append-only `Source Revisions` in the sealed Run determine invalidated bindings; archive files are historical evidence only. Old files, approvals, replies and presentations never authorize renewal. Draft and record the affected sources through their current owners, present them afresh and obtain new deliberate approvals.
+- UR revision requires fresh post-UR Review/Mode and required UX. Later source revision retains only reviewed exact applicable analytical inputs; reassessment routes existing owners before dependent source authoring. Every approved-source revision clears preparation, CD+Tests and review fulfillment; retained code/tests require fresh assessment under the renewed TP. Read-only inspection never recovers. Use explicit `--inspect`/`--recover` for the exact pending operation; a replay reports its historical effect separately from current state and grants no approval.
 - `Approval: SD` permits Task/Test Plan drafting, not implementation.
 - New SD drafts from sd-definition declare sd-decisions-v1 with same-artifact Design Decisions.
   Material before_sd decisions must be resolved with named owners before presentation/approval.
